              "text": "Masticatory—may require liquid food or gruel until jaw mobility is regained; may need a gastric feeding tube to facilitate fluid and caloric intake.",
              "pdf_page": 1021,
              "printed_page": 939,
              "column": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "CLIENT EDUCATION": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "canonical_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Warn client that long-term corticosteroid therapy may be required.",
              "pdf_page": 1021,
              "printed_page": 939,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Inform client that residual muscle atrophy and restricted jaw movement may occur with chronic masticatory muscle disease.",
              "pdf_page": 1021,
              "printed_page": 939,
              "column": 3
            }
          ]
        },
